"q-31402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})|+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{4}^{16}\\frac{2}{x{log}_{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{4}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{16}\\frac{2}{x{log}_{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{log}_{4}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =4{ln}^{2}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d4bd8d8457e7f0bda96f3b9dd270f7d5fcd27a8ef6617ca039f8939171431e" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha256" "a327107e917adda7c7748e617fca468d99eec5fb29bfa4fe429923a8398cafeb" "basis" 1193 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028699/state.json" "file_sha25