category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{3}\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-114020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\cdot {log}_{6}^{3}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{4}^{16}\\frac{2}{x{log}_{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{4}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{16}\\frac{2}{x{log}_{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{log}_{4}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =4{ln}^{2}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "4{ln}^{2}⁡2"] ["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "8{ln}^{2}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{ln}^{2}⁡2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | ${e}^{2}$ | ${e}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87"} {"question" "q-31639" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31639" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{x}{2}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31639" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/2$ | $1/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{1/2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\sqrt{u}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{1}-\\sqrt{0}) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87"} {"question" "q-31643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-31643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{3}^{21}\\frac{1}{x}{log}_{7}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u={log}_{7}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $21$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{21}\\frac{1}{x}{log}_{7}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{21}{log}_{7}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{2}\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87"} {"question" "q-73658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡7"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡7"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{4}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-73658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-13842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-13842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x).$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $e$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e} \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {u}^{2}|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}((\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e)^{2}-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-13842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "88b04a28acd4d8c79e101e9c9e9690d5266f0dc014b1b37dc30f9e50b76e5a87"} {"question" "q-13842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-13842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}((\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e)^{2}-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)^{2})"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}((\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e)^{2}-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)^{2})"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e)^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "q-13842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}((\\operatorname{ln}⁡4e)^{2}-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)^{2})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/state.json" "file_sha256" "09fb5629ced1afa28a441d803c8bf8cd089f79ef936550a076f434fd474f55a9"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "2cc85fe9c460f9351375a20b0c5d037ab2482bb1b0648d80857a1becb926c86e"} {"question" "e-14405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/example-14405.json" "file_sha256" "2cc85fe9c460f9351375a20b0c5d037ab2482bb1b0648d80857a1becb926c86e"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "dbe57670314d8113b536dd73dc121fd43b6e0852c3e160722b325ffd71c116a3"} {"question" "e-14406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/example-14406.json" "file_sha256" "dbe57670314d8113b536dd73dc121fd43b6e0852c3e160722b325ffd71c116a3"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "278fdc27dc2aa71e3861bbf0a0d4ba2d2007ce8fd5062f66273f8922f6ca72a0"} {"question" "e-14422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039202/example-14422.json" "file_sha256" "278fdc27dc2aa71e3861bbf0a0d4ba2d2007ce8fd5062f66273f8922f6ca72a0"}] "usage" {"q-210742" [] "q-73655" [] "e-14422" [] "q-73659" [] "e-14406" [] "q-31398" [] "q-13814" [] "q-31401" [] "q-31402" [] "e-14405" []} "basis" 1350 "retractions" [[17592186101058 :question/problem "Calculate the integral $∫(5)/(x\\ln^{2} (3x))dx$."] [17592186101444 :question/problem "What is $∫(1)/(x\\log_{7} (4x))dx$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186098119 17592186098120 17592